 the physical universe but in a  fluid bio verse and at the center of the  black galaxy lies ego and right away  ego puts a demonstration of what he is  capable of after declaring that his  powers are endless he changes his  surface to include a face that he can  converse with Thor and then Terra forms  himself to reassemble Asgard knowing  that Thor will find those surroundings  more familiar now in doing this he  demonstrates the ability to manipulate  matter on a molecular level ego is also  able to create a humanoid life-form  based on Thor's molecular structure out  of egos own antibodies and states that  his plan is to create billions of them  to aid him in his newfound quest to  conquer the universe however by the end  of his first encounter with Thor he's  defeated and those never to leave his  blot galaxy or try to conquer the cosmos  again but of course that doesn't last  because nothing ever does in comic books  and so for decades we didn't really know  much about egos origins but all that  changed in 2010 during the astonishing  Thor miniseries by Rob rody once  revealed that ego was actually created  by the cosmic entity known as the  stranger who's basically a universal  scientist now in order to create a  living planet the stranger needed  materials belonging to the collector and  in exchange for allowing him to use  those materials the stranger agreed to  create a second living planet for the  collector to keep in his museum now the  stranger agreed and created both ego who  would live his life with autonomy and  alter ego who would be kept in isolation  within a pocket universe in the  collectors museum now the stranger also  reveals that when he created ego he gave  him his own personality and force of  will hence why he decided to name him  ego furthermore after the stranger  informs ego of the existence of his twin  he imbues him with the ability to travel  through hyperspace thereby increasing  his power level even further but even  with that new information  EKOS full origin had not been revealed  and we learned even more about him  during a Ewing's recent Ultimates to run  and so what we learned here is that The  Strangers experiment had created ego and  alter ego had actually used two planets  that orbited the same star and that on  one of those planets village' scientists  named a gross now when the stranger  caused the Sun to explode all the  inhabitants of egress his planet  including himself died and his  consciousness became the consciousness  of ego and this is all revealed during a  conversation with Galactus who at this  point is not the devourer of worlds but  a life bringer and so with egos origins  sounds familiar  it's probably because it's similar to  Galactus as origin who was formerly the  scientist known as Galan now the two of  them even find a form of kinship over  their similarity and Galactus eventually  gives ego a physical body transforming  him into a new version of himself known  as ego pran and so now that we finally  got an egos origin explained we can  finally move on to what his powers are  kind of a fun fact though there was one  point in Marvel Comics when Galactus  ended up strapping a rocket to the  ascend of ego and sent him flying  through the universe it was hilarious  and so having said that I've already has  discussed a few of egos powers and  telling his origin story for instance we  discussed his ability to manipulate  matter and also tear form his own  surface into whatever manner he chooses  he can also create whatever weather he  desires creates shields to protect  himself from damage and reach out into  space with large tentacles capable of  destroying spacecraft that vent  too close to him and not really a power  but more of an aspect of his physiology  ego can absorb beings and digest them  but we also discussed that he can create  a seemingly unlimited number of humanoid  antibodies that defend ego from any  intruders much like the antibodies that  we have i